  offerLine: Snff. Snff snff. That smells like... Nana's kitchen! Where did you find that? Give it here!
  activeLine: The muddy scribble! Bring it here, bring it here!
  readyLine: 'It IS Nana''s! Her truffle toast, in her own muddy writing. I thought it was lost forever. I''m keeping it under my pillow. You have these: Grandad''s two shiniest lumps of kauri gum, and Nana''s golden lights. She''d want them somewhere cosy.'
  doneLine: Nana would have liked you. You smell like toast.
